The '''M176/M177/M178''' is a [[petrol]] [[V8 engine]] range designed by [[Mercedes-AMG]], replacing the [[Mercedes-Benz M278 engine|M278]] and [[Mercedes-Benz M157 engine|M157 engines]], and is based on the [[Mercedes-Benz M133 engine|M133 engine]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.autoevolution.com/news/mercedes-amg-gt-m178-engine-specs-unveiled-videophoto-gallery-82472.html |title=Mercedes-AMG GT M178 Engine Specs Unveiled |first=Alex |last=Oagana |work=Auto Evolution |date=13 June 2014}}</ref>

The engine has two [[BorgWarner]] [[turbocharger]]s positioned between the two [[cylinder head]]s in a [[Hot vee turbocharged engine|"hot-V" configuration]]. The fuel injection system uses [[Bosch (company)|Bosch's]] new [[Piezoelectricity|piezo-electric]] direct fuel injectors that deliver five squirts of fuel per combustion cycle.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.caranddriver.com/news/a15361914/in-depth-with-the-2016-mercedes-amg-gts-new-v-8-so-long-natural-aspiration-hello-twin-turbos/ |title=In-Depth With the 2016 Mercedes-AMG GT's New V-8: So Long, Natural Aspiration—Hello, Twin Turbos! |date=2 July 2014 |work=Car and Driver |first=Don |last=Sherman}}</ref>

The M176 engines are mostly assembled by machine with some components assembled by technicians at [[Untertürkheim]] manufacturing center outside Stuttgart. The M177 and M178 are individually assembled by the technicians in "one man, one engine" principle at the AMG manufacturing center in [[Affalterbach]].<ref>{{cite web|url= http://blog.mercedes-benz-passion.com/2016/10/mercedes-benz-bringt-2017-neue-generation-von-vier-und-sechszylinder-reihenmotoren-bei-benzin-und-diesel-auf-den-markt/ |title=Ab 2017 neue Generation von 4- und 6-Zylinder Reihenmotoren bei Benzin und Diesel |accessdate=18 May 2021 |first=Philipp |last=Deppe |work=mbPassion |date=28 October 2016 }}</ref>

== M176 ==
The M176 version debuted in 2015 for the Mercedes-Benz G 500/G 550 and G 500 4x4<sup>2</sup>. In 2019, M176 was equipped with EQ Boost mild hybrid 48V electrical system, producing additional output {{convert|16|kW|PS|0|abbr=on}} and {{convert|250|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}} of torque.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://media.daimler.com/marsMediaSite/en/instance/ko/The-new-V8-with-48V-ISG-Excitement-on-velvet-paws.xhtml?oid=43613231 |title=The new V8 with 48V ISG: Excitement on velvet paws |accessdate=18 May 2021 |work=Daimler AG Media}}</ref> This mild hybrid system was fitted to GLE 580 4MATIC and GLS 580 4MATIC. The M176 engine with EQ Boost has been upgraded in 2021 for S 580 4MATIC with increased output for petrol engine ({{convert|370|kW|PS bhp|abbr=on|0}}) and decreased output for EQ Boost ({{convert|15|kW|PS|0|abbr=on}}).

